  "equipment_type": "Room sensor / operator unit",
  "applies_to": "Regin Regio RUX room units (temperature, CO2, humidity, VOC sensing with display) with firmware 2.1.",
  "summary": "Regio RUX is a room unit with display and sensors in the Regio family, connected over RS485 (EXOline, Modbus or BACnet MS/TP). The variable list gives 83 BACnet objects: room temperature, CO2, humidity and VOC readings, state setpoints and offset, fan selection, remote values with enable selectors, CO2 LED limits and display settings.",
  "bacnet_transport": [
    "BACnet MS/TP"
  ],
  "firmware": "2.1-1-xx",
  "default_device_instance": null,
  "access_inferred": false,
  "notes": [
    "Taken from Regin's variable list (xlsx), \"Default BACnet name\", \"Object type\", \"Instance\", \"Unit\" and \"Writeable\" columns; the same file lists the EXOline and Modbus addresses.",
    "Names follow the variable list's \"Default BACnet name\" column. Regin's EDE zip for RCX/RTX/RUX 2.1-1-01 holds only an RCX file, which uses upper-case names (for example REG_CONTROLLERSTATE) and repeats instances, so it was not used for names.",
    "Multistate state texts come from the RCX EDE state-text file (matched by instance or object name); the variable list does not print them."
  ],
